# Corpus unit what-will-my-model-forget/C01 — gap (mandatory variance CQ unmet)
#
# Source: m0/annotations/what-will-my-model-forget.yaml C01 (comparative, controlled_comparison;
# corpus pin 62e9b54). Headline: representation-based forecasting achieves the best overall
# forecasting performance — representation-with-prior attains the highest binary F1 in 7 of 8
# Table 1 (model, dataset, tuning) configurations, the lone exception being fixed-logit 68.37 vs
# 67.81 on FLAN-T5Large head tuning (E01, Table 1, section 5.1).
#
# Lowering notes (conventions: corpus-units/LOWERING.md):
#   * controlled_comparison(S, B, Q, D, Exp), conclusion better(S, B, Q, D). Nearest-competitor
#     convention: the binding comparand is fixed_logit (the single method that beats representation
#     in the one exceptional column, hence the tightest competitor); the other three baselines
#     (threshold, trainable_logit, representation-without-prior) and the 7-of-8 count stay in nl
#     and refs. D = forgetting_configs names the 8 enumerated configurations.
#   * The mandatory variance_reported CQ maps onto the annotation's mandatory "are F1 scores
#     reported with seeds or uncertainty so per-column argmax is stable?" — annotated unmet-gap
#     (no repeated runs, seeds, or intervals; several margins are small, e.g. 67.81 vs 68.37). An
#     open mandatory obligation is IncompleteArgument, so NO complete arg is declarable: E2-style
#     gap.
#   * baseline_parity (baseline run in every config) and measurement_validity (one shared pipeline,
#     binary F1 scored identically) are annotated met; scope_match (the single exception config
#     identified and consistent with scope) is annotated met and maps onto corpus-v1's optional
#     scope_match. Their leaves are supplied. Per-method hyperparameter-tuning parity is
#     optional-unmet, no effect.
#   * Leaf kinds are attested (Table 1 cells cited via trace N04/N07/N08/N10/N11, read from the
#     paper's table rather than independently observed).
#
# Expected verdict is at the bottom of this file (golden oracle).

artifact what-will-my-model-forget at sha256:d5369ef41c64
policy corpus-v1
use backends [nd@1]

# --- The headline claim, stated but not assemblable at corpus-v1's evidential bar --------------

claim c01
  nl      = "Representation-with-prior forecasting attains the highest binary F1 in 7 of 8 Table 1 (model, dataset, tuning) configurations, the lone exception being fixed-logit 68.37 vs 67.81 on FLAN-T5Large head tuning; no seeds or uncertainty are reported for the Table 1 cells so the per-column argmax rests on single runs"
  formal  = better(representation_with_prior, fixed_logit, forecasting_f1, forgetting_configs)
  binding = { author = m0-annotator, audit-status = unreviewed }

# --- Evidence leaves are present ... ------------------------------------------------------------

# Principal premise: Table 1's per-configuration F1 argmax (representation-with-prior best in 7/8),
# per result cell, with the fixed-logit exception folded into refs.
leaf e1 : reports(e01, compares(representation_with_prior, fixed_logit, forecasting_f1, forgetting_configs, favorable))
  kind       = attested
  provenance = ai-executed
  refs       = [logic/claims.md#C01, logic/experiments.md#E01-Metrics, trace/exploration_tree.yaml#N10, trace/exploration_tree.yaml#N04, Table-1]

leaf e2 : matched_setup(representation_with_prior, fixed_logit, e01)
  kind       = attested
  provenance = ai-executed
  refs       = [logic/experiments.md#E01-Baselines, logic/experiments.md#E01-Procedure-step-4]

leaf e3 : valid_measurement(forecasting_f1, e01)
  kind       = attested
  provenance = ai-executed
  refs       = [logic/experiments.md#E01-Procedure-step-1, logic/experiments.md#E01-Metrics]

leaf e4 : scope_matched(representation_with_prior, forecasting_f1, forgetting_configs)
  kind       = attested
  provenance = ai-executed
  refs       = [logic/experiments.md#E01-Expected-outcome, trace/exploration_tree.yaml#N04]

# --- ... but no complete argument is declarable -------------------------------------------------

# (Intentionally no `arg`: variance_reported(e01) has no honest leaf — single-run F1 per cell, no
# seeds or intervals, with sub-point margins carrying the 7-of-8 count — and controlled_comparison
# makes that obligation mandatory. The complete-support set is therefore empty.)

status c01

